# The keys makable-shorts uses, and where to get each. `makable-shorts keys --open` writes the ones your choices
# need (`makable-shorts me --filmer ... --narrator ...`) into ~/.config/makable-shorts/.env (SHORTS_HOME's .env)
# and opens it for you to fill in: you needn't copy this file. In a checkout of the repo, .env here works too (git
# ignores it). The environment wins over these files, and SHORTS_HOME's over this folder's.
# One KEY=value a line; a # starts a comment only at the start of a line.

# Where your own things are kept: your photo, music and voice, and your choices (makable-shorts me), each product's
# notes, and the sites you've signed in to (makable-shorts signin). Set it in the environment, since it says where
# this file is.
# SHORTS_HOME=~/.config/makable-shorts

# Who films your intro and outro (me --filmer; run.json's intro and outro; shorts/filmers.py).
# Gemini Omni (omni) films in your own Google Cloud project, on Agent Platform (Vertex AI): one with billing, and the
# Vertex AI API on (gcloud services enable aiplatform.googleapis.com). Sign in to it once, with
# `gcloud auth application-default login`; GitHub Actions signs in with google-github-actions/auth instead.
GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT=
# HeyGen (heygen): an API key from app.heygen.com (Settings, API), paid from its API balance. Its voice is
# me --filmer-voice, from makable-shorts voices.
# HEYGEN_API_KEY=
# Clips you film elsewhere and bring in (import) need no key, and nor does a video with no avatar (none).

# Who speaks the narration (me --narrator; run.json's narrator; shorts/speech_api.py).
# ElevenLabs (elevenlabs): an API key from elevenlabs.io (Developers, API keys), on a plan that can clone a voice.
ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=
# Or your own voice API on Modal (modal): services/voice, deployed to your Modal account by
# `makable-shorts deploy-voice`, which writes these two.
# SHORTS_SPEECH_URL=
# SHORTS_SPEECH_KEY=
# Kokoro (kokoro), on this machine, and no voice at all (none) need no key.

# The Python of browser-use's own environment (it pins its own packages), in a checkout of the repo: the plugin's
# makable-shorts makes its own, in ~/.cache/makable-shorts/envs.
# SHORTS_BROWSE_PYTHON=~/browse-env/bin/python
